ondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and  intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common   communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "The Zero Conditional", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the zero conditional to talk about general truths and   certainties and to give instructions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are two parts to the sentence.<br /> One part is the condition. The other part is the result.  When you want to give an instruction, use the imperative in the main   clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Form:<br /> <span class=\"italic\"> If or When + subject + the Simple Present Tense/Imperative.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can flip the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes  first.<br /><br /><span class=\"italic\">  Subject + the Simple Present tense/Imperative + if or when +   subject + the Simple Present</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Condition</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Result</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you read some books,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">you can learn about African traditions.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Result</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Condition</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">My eyes hurt</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">when I don't have  my glasses.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Notice that you only need a comma (,) if you say the condition first.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "&nbsp;", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Legends vs. Myths", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Legends and myths are types of stories.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A legend is a story that is based on facts, something that happened  in history. It can be about a person.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A myth is a story that is made up or invented. It is a traditional story.   They are about animals or gods. Myths are about how something   happened.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What are popular legends and myths in your country?", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "character ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person or animal in a story ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are there many characters in myths?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use use to talk about stories.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "title ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the name of a specific book ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you know the title of the book?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le08ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "author ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who writes a book ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "typ